Additional Rules
Defensive Roles: There are some defensive roles (e.g. Runner, Scared Werewolf) that require the Host to be aware of their identity. In these cases, the Host can either choose to check cards at the start of the game, wake up the defensive roles one by one in Night 1 to check their identity, or discreetly check cards of players that may die at the end of night before waking the villagers. The Host may take notes if neccesary.
Role Change: There are some roles that can cause role changes. When playing with one of these roles you can choose to have each player check their own card each morning, or wake up players to inform them of their role changes. Roles that don't know when they may change (e.g. Apprentice, Cursed Civilian) and roles targeted for changing by other players (e.g. Infecting Werewolf, Vampire, Thief) can be woken up with a touch on the shoulder. Players should learn this info at the end of night/start of day.
